{
  "id": "fluency-l9-undo-chain",
  "lesson": "l9-undo-chain",
  "title": "Fluency: substitution",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 12,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "power-inside",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "substitute for the inside of a power",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [1, 12] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "n": { "int": [2, 5] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "n1": "n + 1", "r": "k/(2*(n + 1))" },
      "prompt": "Find $\\int {k:c}{v}({v}^2{b:+})^{{{n}}}\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{r:cfrac}({v}^2{b:+})^{{{n1}}}", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "half-missed", "tex": "{2*r:cfrac}({v}^2{b:+})^{{{n1}}}", "line": "With $u = {v}^2{b:+}$, $du = 2{v}\\,d{v}$, so ${k:c}{v}\\,d{v}$ is ${k/2:cfrac}\\,du$: you lost the 2." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "tex": "{k/2:cfrac}({v}^2{b:+})^{{{n1}}}", "line": "You raised the power to {n1} but did not divide by {n1}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Let $u = {v}^2{b:+}$, so $du = 2{v}\\,d{v}$ and ${k:c}{v}\\,d{v} = {k/2:cfrac}\\,du$.",
        "$\\int {k/2:cfrac}u^{{{n}}}\\,du = {r:cfrac}u^{{{n1}}} + C$.",
        "Put $u$ back: ${r:cfrac}({v}^2{b:+})^{{{n1}}} + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exp-inside",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "substitute for the power of e",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "a": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "r": "k/(2*a)" },
      "prompt": "Find $\\int {k:c}{v}e^{{{a:c}{v}^2}}\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{r:cfrac}e^{{{a:c}{v}^2}}", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "half-missed", "tex": "{2*r:cfrac}e^{{{a:c}{v}^2}}", "line": "With $u = {a:c}{v}^2$, $du = {2*a}{v}\\,d{v}$: you divided by {a} but not by 2." },
        { "id": "multiplied", "tex": "{2*a*k}e^{{{a:c}{v}^2}}", "line": "You multiplied by ${2*a}$ instead of dividing by it." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Let $u = {a:c}{v}^2$, so $du = {2*a}{v}\\,d{v}$ and ${k:c}{v}\\,d{v} = {r:cfrac}\\,du$.",
        "$\\int {r:cfrac}e^u\\,du = {r:cfrac}e^u + C = {r:cfrac}e^{{{a:c}{v}^2}} + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "log-inside",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "spot the bottom's derivative on top",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [1, 12] },
        "b": { "int": [1, 9] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "r": "k/2" },
      "prompt": "Find $\\displaystyle\\int \\frac{{{k:c}{v}}}{{{v}^2+{b}}}\\,d{v}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{r:cfrac}\\ln({v}^2+{b})", "upToConstant": true, "keyboard": "calculus" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "half-missed", "tex": "{k:c}\\ln({v}^2+{b})", "line": "With $u = {v}^2+{b}$, $du = 2{v}\\,d{v}$: you lost the 2." },
        { "id": "multiplied", "tex": "{2*k}\\ln({v}^2+{b})", "line": "You multiplied by 2. Since $du = 2{v}\\,d{v}$, divide by 2: ${k:c}{v}\\,d{v} = {r:cfrac}\\,du$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Let $u = {v}^2+{b}$, so $du = 2{v}\\,d{v}$ and ${k:c}{v}\\,d{v} = {r:cfrac}\\,du$.",
        "${r:cfrac}\\int \\frac{{1}}{{u}}\\,du = {r:cfrac}\\ln u + C$, and $u > 0$, so the answer is ${r:cfrac}\\ln({v}^2+{b}) + C$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "definite-power",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "change the limits and evaluate",
      "vars": {
        "m": { "int": [1, 4] },
        "b": { "int": [-3, 4], "not": [0] },
        "np": { "pick": [[1, ""], [2, "^{2}"], [3, "^{3}"]], "as": ["n", "pw"] },
        "p": { "int": [0, 1] },
        "q": { "int": [1, 2] }
      },
      "let": {
        "k": "2*m",
        "n1": "n + 1",
        "lo": "p^2 + b",
        "hi": "q^2 + b",
        "ans": "m*((q^2 + b)^(n + 1) - (p^2 + b)^(n + 1))/(n + 1)",
        "kept": "m*(q^(n + 1) - p^(n + 1))/(n + 1)"
      },
      "where": ["p < q", "(q^2 + b)^(n + 1) <= 256", "kept != ans", "ans != 0"],
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int_{{{p}}}^{{{q}}} {k}x(x^2{b:+}){pw}\\,dx$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "accept": "${ans:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.0005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "limits-kept", "value": "{kept}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "You kept the $x$ limits {p} and {q}. In $u$ they become {lo} and {hi}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Let $u = x^2{b:+}$, so $du = 2x\\,dx$. The limits become $u = {lo}$ and $u = {hi}$.",
        "The integral is ${m:c}\\int_{{{lo}}}^{{{hi}}} {mono(u; 1, n)}\\,du = {m:c}\\left[\\frac{{u^{{{n1}}}}}{{{n1}}}\\right]_{{{lo}}}^{{{hi}}} = {ans:frac}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
